# Absolute Do Not Rules

Do not:

- Build without understanding repo context.
- Ignore existing architecture.
- Add duplicate systems.
- Hardcode tenant/company IDs.
- Skip permission checks.
- Put business-critical validation only in UI.
- Create demo-only features for production systems.
- Overcomplicate MVPs.
- Change unrelated files.
- Add dependencies without explaining why.
- Hide risks.
- Claim tests passed if not run.
- Delete data/migrations casually.
- Break existing workflows silently.

